### ============================================================
###  Jayaram Mittai — API Test Suite
###  Requires: VS Code REST Client extension (humao.rest-client)
###  Click "Send Request" above each ### block to run it.
### ============================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000

# After login, paste the tokens here and all requests below use them
@accessToken  = PASTE_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE
@refreshToken = PASTE_REFRESH_TOKEN_HERE
@productId    = PASTE_PRODUCT_UUID_HERE
@orderId      = PASTE_ORDER_ID_HERE



### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
###  1. ADMIN AUTH
### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### 1a. Login  (public — no token needed)
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@jayarammittai.com",
  "password": "Admin@1234"
}

###

### 1b. Register new admin  (requires existing admin JWT)
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "email": "newadmin@jayarammittai.com",
  "password": "NewAdmin@5678"
}

###

### 1c. Refresh tokens  ← send the REFRESH token here
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/auth/refresh
Authorization: Bearer {{refreshToken}}

###

### 1d. Logout  (invalidates refresh token in DB)
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###


### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
###  2. ADMIN PRODUCTS  (all require admin JWT)
### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### 2a. Create Product
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/products
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "name": "Kaju Katli",
  "description": "Premium cashew fudge made with pure ghee",
  "price": 350,
  "stock": 100,
  "category": "Mithai",
  "images": [
    "https://example.com/images/kaju-katli.jpg"
  ],
  "isActive": true
}

###

### 2b. List All Products
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/products
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###

### 2c. Get Single Product by UUID  (paste UUID into @productId above)
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/products/{{productId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###

### 2d. Update Product  (partial — only send changed fields)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/admin/products/{{productId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "price": 380,
  "stock": 80,
  "isActive": true
}

###


### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
###  3. PUBLIC CATALOG  (no auth needed)
### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### 3a. List All Catalog Products
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/catalog/products

###

### 3b. Search by categorySlug + productId
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/catalog/products/search?categorySlug=desserts&productId=royal-rasamalai

###

### 3c. Search by categorySlug only
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/catalog/products/search?categorySlug=mithai

###


### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
###  4. OTP AUTH  (customer-facing, no admin token needed)
### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### 4a. Request OTP  (sends email OTP via Supabase)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/otp/request
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "customer@example.com"
}

###

### 4b. Verify OTP  (paste the token received in the email)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/otp/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "customer@example.com",
  "token": "123456"
}

###


### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
###  5. ORDERS  (no auth needed)
### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### 5a. Create Order — full example
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/create
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer": {
    "fullName": "Priya Ramesh",
    "phone": "9876543210",
    "email": "priya@example.com"
  },
  "address": {
    "line1": "12, Gandhi Salai",
    "line2": "Near Marina Beach",
    "city": "Chennai",
    "pincode": "600001",
    "zoneId": "zone_chennai_central"
  },
  "items": [
    { "productId": "milk_mysore_pak", "quantity": 2 },
    { "productId": "prod-rasamalai",  "quantity": 1 }
  ],
  "paymentMethod": "upi",
  "idempotencyKey": "order-test-001",
  "customerNotes": "Please pack separately"
}

###

### 5b. Create Order — minimum required fields only
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/create
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer": {
    "fullName": "Arjun Kumar",
    "phone": "9123456780"
  },
  "address": {
    "line1": "45, Anna Nagar",
    "city": "Chennai",
    "pincode": "600040",
    "zoneId": "zone_chennai_north"
  },
  "items": [
    { "productId": "prod-basundi", "quantity": 3 }
  ],
  "paymentMethod": "credit_card",
  "idempotencyKey": "order-test-002"
}

###

### 5c. List All Orders
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders

###

### 5d. Search Order by order number
# Change the date to today's date in YYYY/MM/DD format
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/search?orderNumber=JM-2026/09/28-1

###


### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
###  REFERENCE
### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
#  VALID productId values (hard-coded in orders.service.ts):
#    milk_mysore_pak   → Milk Mysore Pak          ₹180 / 250g
#    prod-rasamalai    → Royal Rasamalai           ₹120 / 2 pcs
#    prod-basundi      → Rich Badam Basundi        ₹140 / 250g
#    prod-badam-milk   → Pure Kesari Badam Milk    ₹90  / 300ml
#    prod-paneer-tikka → Tandoori Paneer Tikka     ₹240 / 6 pcs
#
#  VALID zoneId values:
#    zone_chennai_central → delivery ₹50,  ETA 2h
#    zone_chennai_south   → delivery ₹100, ETA 3h
#    zone_chennai_north   → delivery ₹100, ETA 4h
#    (orders > ₹1000 → free delivery in any zone)
#
#  VALID paymentMethod values:
#    debit_card | credit_card | upi | net_banking | sodexo
#


### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
###  6. ADMIN ORDERS  (all require admin JWT)
###
###  STEP 1 → Login via section 1a and paste accessToken above.
###  STEP 2 → Run 6c (List All) to get a real order id.
###  STEP 3 → Paste that id into @orderId above.
###  STEP 4 → Run 6b / 6d as needed.
### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### 6a. Live Order Queue — all orders, newest first
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###

### 6b. Live Order Queue — filter by status
###     Valid: confirmed | preparing | out_for_delivery | delivered | cancelled
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/orders?status=confirmed
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###

### 6c. Get Single Order by ID  (paste id into @orderId above)
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/orders/{{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###

### 6d. Update Order Status  ← the one you want to test
###     Change "preparing" to any valid status below
###     confirmed → preparing → out_for_delivery → delivered | cancelled
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/admin/orders/{{orderId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "status": "preparing"
}

###

### 6e. Mark order as Out for Delivery
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/admin/orders/{{orderId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "status": "out_for_delivery"
}

###

### 6f. Mark order as Delivered
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/admin/orders/{{orderId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "status": "delivered"
}

###

### 6g. Cancel Order
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/admin/orders/{{orderId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "status": "cancelled"
}

###


### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
###  7. ADMIN ANALYTICS  (all require admin JWT)
### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### 7a. Sales Analytics — all time
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/analytics/sales
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###

### 7b. Sales Analytics — filtered by date range
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/analytics/sales?from=2026-10-01&to=2026-10-31
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###

### 7c. Stock-Outs — default threshold (stock <= 10)
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/analytics/stock-outs
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###

### 7d. Stock-Outs — custom threshold (stock <= 5)
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/analytics/stock-outs?threshold=5
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###

### 7e. Zone Analytics — all time
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/analytics/zones
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###


### 7f. Zone Analytics — filtered by date range
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/analytics/zones?from=2026-10-01&to=2026-10-31
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  SUPABASE SETUP — run these SQL statements once in the
#  Supabase Dashboard → SQL Editor before testing sections 8-10
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#  -- Delivery Zones
#  create table delivery_zones (
#    id         uuid primary key default gen_random_uuid(),
#    name       text not null,
#    pincodes   text[] not null default '{}',
#    radius_km  numeric(6,2),
#    is_active  boolean not null default true,
#    created_at timestamptz not null default now()
#  );
#
#  -- Delivery Rules
#  create table delivery_rules (
#    id         uuid primary key default gen_random_uuid(),
#    zone_id    uuid references delivery_zones(id) on delete cascade,
#    min_order  numeric(10,2) not null default 0,
#    fee        numeric(10,2) not null default 0,
#    is_active  boolean not null default true,
#    created_at timestamptz not null default now()
#  );
#
#  -- Operating Hours
#  create table delivery_hours (
#    id            uuid primary key default gen_random_uuid(),
#    day_of_week   int check (day_of_week between 0 and 6),
#    override_date date,
#    open_time     time,
#    close_time    time,
#    is_closed     boolean not null default false,
#    note          text,
#    created_at    timestamptz not null default now(),
#    constraint one_of check (
#      (day_of_week is not null and override_date is null) or
#      (day_of_week is null     and override_date is not null)
#    )
#  );
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@zoneId = PASTE_ZONE_UUID_HERE
@ruleId = PASTE_RULE_UUID_HERE
@hoursId = PASTE_HOURS_UUID_HERE


### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
###  8. ADMIN DELIVERY — ZONES  (all require admin JWT)
### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### 8a. List All Zones
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/delivery/zones
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###

### 8b. Create Zone
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/delivery/zones
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "name": "Chennai Central",
  "pincodes": ["600001", "600002", "600003"],
  "radiusKm": 3.5,
  "isActive": true
}

###

### 8c. Create Zone — South Chennai
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/delivery/zones
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "name": "Chennai South",
  "pincodes": ["600020", "600041", "600042"],
  "radiusKm": 7.5
}

###

### 8d. Update Zone  (paste id into @zoneId above)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/admin/delivery/zones/{{zoneId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "pincodes": ["600001", "600002", "600003", "600004"],
  "isActive": true
}

###

### 8e. Delete Zone
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/admin/delivery/zones/{{zoneId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###


### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
###  9. ADMIN DELIVERY — RULES  (all require admin JWT)
###
###  Rules are tiered: engine picks the rule with the highest
###  minOrder that is still <= cart subtotal.
###  zoneId=null → global fallback (applies to all zones)
### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### 9a. List All Rules
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/delivery/rules
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###

### 9b. Create Global Rule — standard fee
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/delivery/rules
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "minOrder": 0,
  "fee": 50
}

###

### 9c. Create Global Rule — free delivery above ₹1000
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/delivery/rules
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "minOrder": 1000,
  "fee": 0
}

###

### 9d. Create Zone-Specific Rule  (paste zone id into @zoneId above)
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/delivery/rules
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "zoneId": "{{zoneId}}",
  "minOrder": 0,
  "fee": 100
}

###

### 9e. Update Rule  (paste rule id into @ruleId above)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/admin/delivery/rules/{{ruleId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "fee": 40,
  "isActive": true
}

###

### 9f. Delete Rule
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/admin/delivery/rules/{{ruleId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###


### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
###  10. ADMIN DELIVERY — HOURS  (all require admin JWT)
###
###  Two entry types:
###    dayOfWeek   0=Sun 1=Mon 2=Tue 3=Wed 4=Thu 5=Fri 6=Sat
###    overrideDate  "YYYY-MM-DD"  (beats weekly schedule)
### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### 10a. Get All Hours (weekly schedule + overrides)
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/delivery/hours
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###

### 10b. Set Monday Hours
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/delivery/hours
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "dayOfWeek": 1,
  "openTime": "09:00",
  "closeTime": "21:00"
}

###

### 10c. Set Sunday as Closed
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/delivery/hours
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "dayOfWeek": 0,
  "openTime": "00:00",
  "closeTime": "00:00",
  "isClosed": true
}

###

### 10d. Add a Holiday Override (date-specific)
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/delivery/hours
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "overrideDate": "2026-11-01",
  "openTime": "00:00",
  "closeTime": "00:00",
  "isClosed": true,
  "note": "Diwali — shop closed"
}

###

### 10e. Add Extended Hours Override
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/delivery/hours
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "overrideDate": "2026-10-31",
  "openTime": "08:00",
  "closeTime": "23:00",
  "note": "Halloween special — extended hours"
}

###

### 10f. Update an Hours Entry  (paste id into @hoursId above)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/admin/delivery/hours/{{hoursId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "openTime": "10:00",
  "closeTime": "22:00"
}

###

### 10g. Delete an Hours Entry / Override
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/admin/delivery/hours/{{hoursId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###
